# Line endings.
#
# The repo is developed partly on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which quietly gave the
# working copy CRLF endings. That is harmless for Rust — rustc reads either — but fatal for a
# shell script: a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line ending in CR names the interpreter `bash\r`, which
# does not exist, and `build-release.sh` copies these files verbatim into the release bundle. A
# CRLF `yos` shipped in the image and every call to it failed with a traceback until it was
# hand-fixed. So the tools that get shipped and executed are pinned to LF here, at the source.

# Executable shell tools — must be LF, they run on Linux.
*.sh              text eol=lf
deploy/yantrik-os/yos          text eol=lf
deploy/yantrik-os/yos-mcp      text eol=lf
deploy/yantrik-os/yantrik-update text eol=lf

# Source and config: normalise to LF in the repo, so a checkout on any platform matches what
# CI and the release build see.
*.rs              text eol=lf
*.slint           text eol=lf
*.toml            text eol=lf
*.yaml            text eol=lf
*.yml             text eol=lf
*.json            text eol=lf
*.md              text eol=lf
